{#
    Override of EasyAdmin's page/content.html.twig.

    EasyAdmin 4.29+ ships a backward-compatibility shim where the "page_title" and
    "content_title" blocks delegate to each other:

        {% block page_title %}{{ block('content_title') }}{% endblock %}
        {% block content_title %}{{ block('page_title') }}{% endblock %}

    That shim is only safe when the concrete page overrides one of those blocks.
    PteroCA panel pages render their own headers inside the "content" block and do
    not define "content_title", which leaves the two blocks delegating to each
    other indefinitely, causing infinite recursion while rendering the page <title>
    (memory exhaustion in Twig's ProfilerExtension / a hung request in production).

    Defining an empty "content_title" here terminates the cycle for every panel page
    while still allowing individual pages to override it when they need a heading.
#}
{% extends '@!EasyAdmin/page/content.html.twig' %}

{% block content_title %}{% endblock %}
